    {
      "id": "r20261023-a02",
      "title": "The Rise of Urban Farming",
      "level": "Menengah atas",
      "min": 4,
      "body": [
        "In many large cities, people are starting to grow food in surprising places: on rooftops, on balconies, and even inside empty buildings. This trend is called urban farming, and it is growing quickly around the world.",
        "Urban farming offers several benefits. It gives city families access to fresh vegetables that have not traveled thousands of kilometers. It also reduces the need for packaging and transport, which means less pollution. For many people, gardening is also a relaxing hobby that improves their mental health.",
        "Of course, there are challenges. City soil can be polluted, so farmers often use clean soil in containers or grow plants in water. Space is limited, and sunlight can be blocked by tall buildings. Still, as technology improves and more people join in, urban farming is likely to become a normal part of city life."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "rooftops": "atap",
        "balconies": "balkon",
        "trend": "tren",
        "packaging": "kemasan",
        "pollution": "polusi",
        "containers": "wadah",
        "likely": "kemungkinan"
      },
